# DbDataSync's integration suites read their connection strings from the variables `env` prints (DBDATAKIT_TEST_MSSQL, _MSSQL_TARGET, _POSTGRES_LOGICAL,
# _POSTGRES_LOGICAL_JDBC_URL, _MYSQL, _MARIADB, _ORACLE; literal defaults in the tests are the values of
# the old DbDataSync/docker-compose.yml, which is gone: password DbDataSync_Test_Pw1, user dbdatasync / root / sa). Start the engines
# the suites need and `eval "$(testenv/testenv.sh env dbdatasync)"`:
#   testenv/testenv.sh up mssql mssql-target postgres-logical mysql mariadb oracle
# Sync's PostgreSQL is the postgres-logical engine (wal_level=logical, wal2json), not the plain `postgres` the other suites use.
